.TH GPHOTO 1 "October 2026" "gPhoto 0.5.0-pre" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gphoto \- the GNU Digital Camera Program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gphoto
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gphoto
downloads, views and manages pictures on digital cameras through
libgphoto2.
.PP
Started without picture or information options, gphoto opens its
window and connects to the first camera it finds.  With any of them it
runs on the command line and exits.
.PP
Pictures are numbered from 1 in folder and file name order, as in the
index window.  A
.I RANGE
is a comma-separated list of numbers and number ranges, such as
.BR 1,3,5-9 ,
or one of the words
.B last
and
.BR all .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Camera selection
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model =\fIMODEL\fR
Camera model, as listed by \fB\-\-list\-cameras\fR.  Default: auto-detect.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port =\fIPORT\fR
Port, for example \fBusb:\fR, \fBserial:/dev/ttyS0\fR, \fBptpip:192.168.1.1\fR
or \fBdisk:/media/card\fR.
.SS Information
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-auto\-detect
List cameras connected to this computer.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-cameras
List every camera model libgphoto2 supports.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-ports
List available ports.
.TP
.BR \-\-summary ", " \-\-manual ", " \-\-about
Show the camera summary, the driver manual or information about the driver.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the gPhoto and libgphoto2 versions.
.SS Pictures
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-num\-pictures
Print the number of pictures on the camera.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List pictures with number, path, size, date and type.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-get =\fIRANGE\fR
Save pictures.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-get\-thumbnail =\fIRANGE\fR
Save thumbnails.  If the camera has none, gphoto makes them.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delete =\fIRANGE\fR
Delete pictures.  Done after saving, so \fB\-s all \-d all\fR moves
everything off the camera.  Asks first; use \fB\-\-force\fR in scripts.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-capture
Take a picture.  With \fB\-o\fR the new picture is saved.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-upload =\fIFILE\fR
Upload a file to the camera.  May be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-folder =\fIFOLDER\fR
Camera folder for \fB\-\-upload\fR.  Default: /.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIPATH\fR
Where to save.  A directory keeps the camera's file names; when more
than one picture is saved the directory is created if needed.
.TP
.BR \-\-html =\fIDIR\fR
Publish an HTML gallery of all pictures, or of \fB\-s\fR \fIRANGE\fR, into \fIDIR\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-title =\fITITLE\fR
Title of the HTML gallery.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Do not ask before deleting.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only what was asked for.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-gui
Never start the graphical interface.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Move every picture to a folder:
.B gphoto \-s all \-d all \-\-force \-o ~/Pictures/2026-10-10
.TP
Browse a memory card as a camera:
.B gphoto \-m "Directory Browse" \-p disk:/media/card
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if a camera operation failed, 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gphoto2 (1)
